[2026-03-14T21:06:09.586Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012RDVYr85msVNgfPCrKXKhx","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information I need. Let me create a comprehensive summary of the app structure for writing sign-up related Playwright tests.\n\n## App Structure Summary for Sign-Up Related Playwright Tests\n\n### 1. APP DIRECTORY STRUCTURE\n\n**Main app location**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/`\n\nKey directories:\n- `/src` - React application source code\n  - `/pages` - Page components\n  - `/components` - React components\n  - `/slices` - Redux slice definitions\n- `/netlify/functions` - Backend API functions\n- `/tests` - Playwright test files\n- `/docs` - Documentation\n- `/scripts` - Build and test automation scripts\n\n### 2. SIGN-UP PAGE & COMPONENT\n\n**Sign-Up Page**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/pages/SignUp.tsx`\n- Route: `/signup`\n- Renders the `SignUpForm` component\n- Redirects authenticated users to `/my-issues`\n- Uses Redux selector to check authentication state\n- Has test ID: `data-testid=\"signup-page\"`\n\n**Sign-Up Form Component**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/SignUpForm.tsx`\n- Collects name, email, and password\n- Client-side validation:\n  - Name: required\n  - Email: required, valid email format (regex: `/^[^\\s@]+@[^\\s@]+\\.[^\\s@]+$/`)\n  - Password: required, minimum 8 characters\n- Dispatches `signup` Redux action\n- Form has test ID: `data-testid=\"signup-form\"`\n- Input field test IDs:\n  - Name: `signup-name-input` with error: `signup-name-error`\n  - Email: `signup-email-input` with error: `signup-email-error`\n  - Password: `signup-password-input` with error: `signup-password-error`\n- Submit button: `signup-submit-button`\n- Link to login: `signup-login-link`\n- Error display: `signup-error`\n\n### 3. AUTH-RELATED NETLIFY FUNCTIONS\n\n**Signup Endpoint**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/signup.ts`\n- **Method**: POST\n- **Endpoint**: `/api/signup`\n- **Request body**:\n  ```json\n  { \"name\": string, \"email\": string, \"password\": string }\n  ```\n- **Response on success (201)**:\n  ```json\n  { \"user\": { \"id\": string, \"name\": string, \"email\": string }, \"token\": string }\n  ```\n- **Error responses**:\n  - 400: Missing required fields, password < 8 characters\n  - 409: Email already exists (\"An account with this email already exists\")\n  - 500: Server error\n- **Behavior**:\n  - Hashes password using PBKDF2 with 10000 iterations, salt stored\n  - Creates member record with role \"admin\"\n  - Creates default workspace if none exists\n  - Creates session token (valid 30 days)\n  - Stores token in sessions table\n\n**Login Endpoint**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/login.ts`\n- **Method**: POST\n- **Endpoint**: `/api/login`\n- **Request body**: `{ \"email\": string, \"password\": string }`\n- **Response on success (200)**: Same as signup\n- **Error responses**:\n  - 400: Missing email or password\n  - 401: Invalid email or password\n  - 500: Server error\n- **Behavior**:\n  - Validates password against stored hash\n  - Creates session token if credentials valid\n\n**Shared DB Module**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/db.ts`\n- Exports `getSql()` function that returns Neon SQL client\n- Uses `@neondatabase/serverless` library\n- Connects via `DATABASE_URL` environment variable\n\n### 4. DATABASE SCHEMA\n\n**Key tables** (from `/repo/apps/LinearClone/scripts/schema.ts`):\n\n**members table**:\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE members (\n  id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n  name TEXT NOT NULL,\n  email TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE,\n  password_hash TEXT NOT NULL,\n  password_salt TEXT NOT NULL,\n  role TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'member',\n  created_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE DEFAULT NOW()\n)\n```\n\n**sessions table**:\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE sessions (\n  token TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n  member_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES members(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n  expires_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE NOT NULL\n)\n```\n\n**workspaces table**:\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE workspaces (\n  id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n  name TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'My Workspace',\n  default_team_id UUID\n)\n```\n\n### 5. EXISTING TEST FILE\n\n**Login Test File**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/tests/login.spec.ts` (8206 bytes)\n\nThe existing login tests cover:\n- Form rendering\n- Successful login with valid credentials\n- Invalid email errors\n- Incorrect password errors\n- Field validation (required fields, email format)\n- Navigation to signup from login\n- Password field masking\n- Enter key submission\n- Redirect for authenticated users\n- Uses test ID selectors extensively\n- Creates test users via API before tests using `fetch('/api/signup', ...)`\n- Uses helper functions: `createTestUser()` and `cleanupTestUsers()`\n- Relies on seeded user `alice@acme.com` with password `password123`\n\n### 6. PLAYWRIGHT CONFIGURATION\n\n**Config File**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/playwright.config.ts`\n- Test directory: `./tests`\n- Timeout: 60000ms globally, 10000ms for expect\n- Base URL: `http://localhost:8888`\n- Action timeout: 15000ms\n- Fully parallel: enabled\n- Reporter: Replay IO (local, no upload) + JSON + HTML\n- Uses Replay Chromium device for debugging\n\n### 7. TEST DATABASE & SEEDING\n\n**Seed Data File**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/scripts/seed-db.ts`\n\nDefault seeded users:\n- **Alice Johnson** - `alice@acme.com` / `password123` (admin role)\n- **Bob Smith** - `bob@acme.com` / `password123` (member role)\n- **Carol Davis** - `carol@acme.com` / `password123` (member role)\n\nSeeded data includes:\n- 2 teams: Engineering (ENG), Design (DES)\n- 1 workspace: Acme Corp\n- Multiple issues, labels, cycles, projects\n- Sample notifications for Alice\n\n**Schema Initialization**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/scripts/schema.ts`\n- Creates all tables with indexes\n- Uses Neon database\n- Idempotent (CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS)\n\n### 8. AUTH STATE MANAGEMENT\n\n**Auth Redux Slice**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/slices/authSlice.ts`\n\nState shape:\n```typescript\ninterface AuthState {\n  user: { id: string; name: string; email: string } | null;\n  token: string | null;\n  loading: boolean;\n  error: string | null;\n}\n```\n\nKey async thunks:\n- `login({ email, password })` - POST to `/api/login`\n- `signup({ name, email, password })` - POST to `/api/signup`\n- `fetchCurrentUser()` - GET to `/api/me` (validates token)\n\nActions:\n- `logout()` - clears state and localStorage\n- `clearError()` - clears error message\n\nToken storage:\n- Stored in `localStorage` as `session_token` key\n- Initialized from localStorage on app start\n- Auto-removed on logout or session expiration\n\n### 9. APP ROUTING & AUTH FLOW\n\n**App Component**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/App.tsx`\n\nProtected routes (require authentication):\n- `/my-issues` - My Issues page\n- `/inbox` - Inbox/Notifications\n- `/team/:teamId/issues` - Team issues\n- `/team/:teamId/cycles` - Team cycles\n- `/issue/:issueId` - Issue detail\n- `/projects` - Projects page\n- `/project/:projectId` - Project detail\n- `/settings/*` - Settings pages\n\nPublic routes:\n- `/login` - Login page\n- `/signup` - Sign-up page\n\nAuth flow:\n1. Unauthenticated users accessing protected routes redirect to `/login`\n2. Authenticated users accessing `/login` or `/signup` redirect to `/my-issues`\n3. Token persists in localStorage across sessions\n4. App layout includes Sidebar, KeyboardShortcuts, CreateIssueModal\n\n### 10. TEST SPECIFICATIONS\n\n**Test Specification Doc**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/docs/tests.md`\n\nSign-up related tests specified (lines 58-111):\n\n1. **Sign up form renders with name, email, and password fields**\n   - Navigate to `/signup` (unauthenticated)\n   - Verify name, email, password fields, \"Create account\" button, \"Log in\" link\n\n2. **Successful account creation**\n   - New email `newuser@test.com`\n   - Fill form and submit\n   - Verify: account created, workspace created, redirect to `/my-issues`, token in localStorage\n\n3. **Sign up fails with existing email**\n   - Use existing email `existing@test.com`\n   - Verify: error message \"An account with this email already exists\"\n   - Remain on signup page\n\n4. **Sign up form validates required fields**\n   - Click \"Create account\" with empty fields\n   - Verify: validation errors for all fields\n\n5. **Sign up form validates email format**\n   - Enter invalid email `bademail`\n   - Verify: email format validation error\n\n6. **Sign up form validates password minimum length**\n   - Enter password < 8 characters\n   - Verify: password too short error\n\n7. **Navigate to login page from sign up**\n   - Click \"Log in\" link\n   - Verify: navigate to `/login`\n\n8. **Password field masks input on sign up**\n   - Verify: password field type is \"password\"\n   - Input is masked\n\n9. **Sign up form can be submitted via Enter key**\n   - Fill form, press Enter on password field\n   - Verify: form submitted (same as clicking button)\n\n10. **Sign up redirects authenticated users**\n    - User has session token in localStorage\n    - Navigate to `/signup`\n    - Verify: redirect to `/my-issues`, no form shown\n\n### 11. TEST RUNNER SETUP\n\n**Test Script**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/scripts/test.ts`\n\nTest execution flow:\n1. Loads `.env` file\n2. Creates ephemeral Neon database branch (test isolation)\n3. Initializes schema on ephemeral DB\n4. Seeds database with test data\n5. Starts `netlify dev` on port 8888\n6. Runs Playwright tests with single worker, no retries\n7. Cleans up ephemeral branch after tests\n8. Uploads failing test recordings to Replay.io\n\nTest invocation:\n```bash\nnpm run test tests/login.spec.ts\n```\n\nEnvironment variables needed:\n- `DATABASE_URL` - Neon database connection string\n- `NEON_API_KEY` - For ephemeral branch creation\n- `NEON_PROJECT_ID` - Neon project ID\n\n### 12. KEY TEST PATTERNS FROM EXISTING LOGIN TESTS\n\n**Helper function pattern**:\n```typescript\nasync function createTestUser(baseURL: string, name: string, email: string, password: string) {\n  const response = await fetch(`${baseURL}/api/signup`, {\n    method: 'POST',\n    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n    body: JSON.stringify({ name, email, password }),\n  });\n  return response.json();\n}\n```\n\n**Test patterns**:\n- Use `test.slow()` for slower tests (login/signup)\n- Use `test.describe()` to group related tests\n- Use `await expect(...).toBeVisible({ timeout: 30000 })` for DOM waits\n- Use `page.getByTestId()` for element selection\n- Use `baseURL` from config for API calls\n- Set localStorage before navigation: `await page.evaluate((t) => localStorage.setItem('session_token', t), token)`\n- Verify redirect: `await expect(page).toHaveURL(/\\/my-issues/)`\n\n### ABSOLUTE FILE PATHS FOR KEY FILES\n\n1. **Sign-up page component**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/pages/SignUp.tsx`\n2. **Sign-up form component**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/SignUpForm.tsx`\n3. **Auth Redux slice**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/slices/authSlice.ts`\n4. **Signup function**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/signup.ts`\n5. **Login function**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/login.ts`\n6. **DB shared module**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/db.ts`\n7. **Database schema**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/scripts/schema.ts`\n8. **Seed data**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/scripts/seed-db.ts`\n9. **Test specification**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/docs/tests.md`\n10. **Playwright config**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/playwright.config.ts`\n11. **Existing login tests**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/tests/login.spec.ts`\n12. **Test runner script**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/scripts/test.ts`\n13. **App routing**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/App.tsx`\n14. **Redux store**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/store.ts`\n15. **Netlify config**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify.toml`\n16. **Package.json** (with test script): `/repo/apps/LinearClone/package.json`\n\nThis comprehensive structure provides everything needed to write thorough Playwright tests for the sign-up feature, following the patterns established in the existing login tests."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: abd0eee55c3201f83 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 56402\ntool_uses: 33\nduration_ms: 52371</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bba55255-5906-4397-88b6-4f0dfb6b6368","uuid":"a65e375b-1ff0-4350-8ef0-8f636865d780","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I need to understand the app structure for writing sign-up related Playwright tests. Find:\n1. The app directory (look in /repo/apps/)\n2. The sign-up page component and related components\n3. The auth-related Netlify functions (signup, login endpoints)\n4. Any existing test files (*.spec.ts)\n5. The docs/tests.md file for test specifications\n6. The playwright config\n7. The database schema (especially users table)\n8. Any seed data files\n9. The netlify/functions/db.ts shared module\n\nBe thorough - read the actual file contents of key files like the signup page component, auth functions, test specs, and existing test files.","agentId":"abd0eee55c3201f83","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information I need. Let me create a comprehensive summary of the app structure for writing sign-up related Playwright tests.\n\n## App Structure Summary for Sign-Up Related Playwright Tests\n\n### 1. APP DIRECTORY STRUCTURE\n\n**Main app location**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/`\n\nKey directories:\n- `/src` - React application source code\n  - `/pages` - Page components\n  - `/components` - React components\n  - `/slices` - Redux slice definitions\n- `/netlify/functions` - Backend API functions\n- `/tests` - Playwright test files\n- `/docs` - Documentation\n- `/scripts` - Build and test automation scripts\n\n### 2. SIGN-UP PAGE & COMPONENT\n\n**Sign-Up Page**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/pages/SignUp.tsx`\n- Route: `/signup`\n- Renders the `SignUpForm` component\n- Redirects authenticated users to `/my-issues`\n- Uses Redux selector to check authentication state\n- Has test ID: `data-testid=\"signup-page\"`\n\n**Sign-Up Form Component**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/SignUpForm.tsx`\n- Collects name, email, and password\n- Client-side validation:\n  - Name: required\n  - Email: required, valid email format (regex: `/^[^\\s@]+@[^\\s@]+\\.[^\\s@]+$/`)\n  - Password: required, minimum 8 characters\n- Dispatches `signup` Redux action\n- Form has test ID: `data-testid=\"signup-form\"`\n- Input field test IDs:\n  - Name: `signup-name-input` with error: `signup-name-error`\n  - Email: `signup-email-input` with error: `signup-email-error`\n  - Password: `signup-password-input` with error: `signup-password-error`\n- Submit button: `signup-submit-button`\n- Link to login: `signup-login-link`\n- Error display: `signup-error`\n\n### 3. AUTH-RELATED NETLIFY FUNCTIONS\n\n**Signup Endpoint**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/signup.ts`\n- **Method**: POST\n- **Endpoint**: `/api/signup`\n- **Request body**:\n  ```json\n  { \"name\": string, \"email\": string, \"password\": string }\n  ```\n- **Response on success (201)**:\n  ```json\n  { \"user\": { \"id\": string, \"name\": string, \"email\": string }, \"token\": string }\n  ```\n- **Error responses**:\n  - 400: Missing required fields, password < 8 characters\n  - 409: Email already exists (\"An account with this email already exists\")\n  - 500: Server error\n- **Behavior**:\n  - Hashes password using PBKDF2 with 10000 iterations, salt stored\n  - Creates member record with role \"admin\"\n  - Creates default workspace if none exists\n  - Creates session token (valid 30 days)\n  - Stores token in sessions table\n\n**Login Endpoint**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/login.ts`\n- **Method**: POST\n- **Endpoint**: `/api/login`\n- **Request body**: `{ \"email\": string, \"password\": string }`\n- **Response on success (200)**: Same as signup\n- **Error responses**:\n  - 400: Missing email or password\n  - 401: Invalid email or password\n  - 500: Server error\n- **Behavior**:\n  - Validates password against stored hash\n  - Creates session token if credentials valid\n\n**Shared DB Module**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/db.ts`\n- Exports `getSql()` function that returns Neon SQL client\n- Uses `@neondatabase/serverless` library\n- Connects via `DATABASE_URL` environment variable\n\n### 4. DATABASE SCHEMA\n\n**Key tables** (from `/repo/apps/LinearClone/scripts/schema.ts`):\n\n**members table**:\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE members (\n  id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n  name TEXT NOT NULL,\n  email TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE,\n  password_hash TEXT NOT NULL,\n  password_salt TEXT NOT NULL,\n  role TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'member',\n  created_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE DEFAULT NOW()\n)\n```\n\n**sessions table**:\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE sessions (\n  token TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n  member_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES members(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n  expires_at TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE NOT NULL\n)\n```\n\n**workspaces table**:\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE workspaces (\n  id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n  name TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'My Workspace',\n  default_team_id UUID\n)\n```\n\n### 5. EXISTING TEST FILE\n\n**Login Test File**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/tests/login.spec.ts` (8206 bytes)\n\nThe existing login tests cover:\n- Form rendering\n- Successful login with valid credentials\n- Invalid email errors\n- Incorrect password errors\n- Field validation (required fields, email format)\n- Navigation to signup from login\n- Password field masking\n- Enter key submission\n- Redirect for authenticated users\n- Uses test ID selectors extensively\n- Creates test users via API before tests using `fetch('/api/signup', ...)`\n- Uses helper functions: `createTestUser()` and `cleanupTestUsers()`\n- Relies on seeded user `alice@acme.com` with password `password123`\n\n### 6. PLAYWRIGHT CONFIGURATION\n\n**Config File**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/playwright.config.ts`\n- Test directory: `./tests`\n- Timeout: 60000ms globally, 10000ms for expect\n- Base URL: `http://localhost:8888`\n- Action timeout: 15000ms\n- Fully parallel: enabled\n- Reporter: Replay IO (local, no upload) + JSON + HTML\n- Uses Replay Chromium device for debugging\n\n### 7. TEST DATABASE & SEEDING\n\n**Seed Data File**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/scripts/seed-db.ts`\n\nDefault seeded users:\n- **Alice Johnson** - `alice@acme.com` / `password123` (admin role)\n- **Bob Smith** - `bob@acme.com` / `password123` (member role)\n- **Carol Davis** - `carol@acme.com` / `password123` (member role)\n\nSeeded data includes:\n- 2 teams: Engineering (ENG), Design (DES)\n- 1 workspace: Acme Corp\n- Multiple issues, labels, cycles, projects\n- Sample notifications for Alice\n\n**Schema Initialization**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/scripts/schema.ts`\n- Creates all tables with indexes\n- Uses Neon database\n- Idempotent (CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS)\n\n### 8. AUTH STATE MANAGEMENT\n\n**Auth Redux Slice**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/slices/authSlice.ts`\n\nState shape:\n```typescript\ninterface AuthState {\n  user: { id: string; name: string; email: string } | null;\n  token: string | null;\n  loading: boolean;\n  error: string | null;\n}\n```\n\nKey async thunks:\n- `login({ email, password })` - POST to `/api/login`\n- `signup({ name, email, password })` - POST to `/api/signup`\n- `fetchCurrentUser()` - GET to `/api/me` (validates token)\n\nActions:\n- `logout()` - clears state and localStorage\n- `clearError()` - clears error message\n\nToken storage:\n- Stored in `localStorage` as `session_token` key\n- Initialized from localStorage on app start\n- Auto-removed on logout or session expiration\n\n### 9. APP ROUTING & AUTH FLOW\n\n**App Component**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/App.tsx`\n\nProtected routes (require authentication):\n- `/my-issues` - My Issues page\n- `/inbox` - Inbox/Notifications\n- `/team/:teamId/issues` - Team issues\n- `/team/:teamId/cycles` - Team cycles\n- `/issue/:issueId` - Issue detail\n- `/projects` - Projects page\n- `/project/:projectId` - Project detail\n- `/settings/*` - Settings pages\n\nPublic routes:\n- `/login` - Login page\n- `/signup` - Sign-up page\n\nAuth flow:\n1. Unauthenticated users accessing protected routes redirect to `/login`\n2. Authenticated users accessing `/login` or `/signup` redirect to `/my-issues`\n3. Token persists in localStorage across sessions\n4. App layout includes Sidebar, KeyboardShortcuts, CreateIssueModal\n\n### 10. TEST SPECIFICATIONS\n\n**Test Specification Doc**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/docs/tests.md`\n\nSign-up related tests specified (lines 58-111):\n\n1. **Sign up form renders with name, email, and password fields**\n   - Navigate to `/signup` (unauthenticated)\n   - Verify name, email, password fields, \"Create account\" button, \"Log in\" link\n\n2. **Successful account creation**\n   - New email `newuser@test.com`\n   - Fill form and submit\n   - Verify: account created, workspace created, redirect to `/my-issues`, token in localStorage\n\n3. **Sign up fails with existing email**\n   - Use existing email `existing@test.com`\n   - Verify: error message \"An account with this email already exists\"\n   - Remain on signup page\n\n4. **Sign up form validates required fields**\n   - Click \"Create account\" with empty fields\n   - Verify: validation errors for all fields\n\n5. **Sign up form validates email format**\n   - Enter invalid email `bademail`\n   - Verify: email format validation error\n\n6. **Sign up form validates password minimum length**\n   - Enter password < 8 characters\n   - Verify: password too short error\n\n7. **Navigate to login page from sign up**\n   - Click \"Log in\" link\n   - Verify: navigate to `/login`\n\n8. **Password field masks input on sign up**\n   - Verify: password field type is \"password\"\n   - Input is masked\n\n9. **Sign up form can be submitted via Enter key**\n   - Fill form, press Enter on password field\n   - Verify: form submitted (same as clicking button)\n\n10. **Sign up redirects authenticated users**\n    - User has session token in localStorage\n    - Navigate to `/signup`\n    - Verify: redirect to `/my-issues`, no form shown\n\n### 11. TEST RUNNER SETUP\n\n**Test Script**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/scripts/test.ts`\n\nTest execution flow:\n1. Loads `.env` file\n2. Creates ephemeral Neon database branch (test isolation)\n3. Initializes schema on ephemeral DB\n4. Seeds database with test data\n5. Starts `netlify dev` on port 8888\n6. Runs Playwright tests with single worker, no retries\n7. Cleans up ephemeral branch after tests\n8. Uploads failing test recordings to Replay.io\n\nTest invocation:\n```bash\nnpm run test tests/login.spec.ts\n```\n\nEnvironment variables needed:\n- `DATABASE_URL` - Neon database connection string\n- `NEON_API_KEY` - For ephemeral branch creation\n- `NEON_PROJECT_ID` - Neon project ID\n\n### 12. KEY TEST PATTERNS FROM EXISTING LOGIN TESTS\n\n**Helper function pattern**:\n```typescript\nasync function createTestUser(baseURL: string, name: string, email: string, password: string) {\n  const response = await fetch(`${baseURL}/api/signup`, {\n    method: 'POST',\n    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n    body: JSON.stringify({ name, email, password }),\n  });\n  return response.json();\n}\n```\n\n**Test patterns**:\n- Use `test.slow()` for slower tests (login/signup)\n- Use `test.describe()` to group related tests\n- Use `await expect(...).toBeVisible({ timeout: 30000 })` for DOM waits\n- Use `page.getByTestId()` for element selection\n- Use `baseURL` from config for API calls\n- Set localStorage before navigation: `await page.evaluate((t) => localStorage.setItem('session_token', t), token)`\n- Verify redirect: `await expect(page).toHaveURL(/\\/my-issues/)`\n\n### ABSOLUTE FILE PATHS FOR KEY FILES\n\n1. **Sign-up page component**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/pages/SignUp.tsx`\n2. **Sign-up form component**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/SignUpForm.tsx`\n3. **Auth Redux slice**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/slices/authSlice.ts`\n4. **Signup function**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/signup.ts`\n5. **Login function**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/login.ts`\n6. **DB shared module**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/db.ts`\n7. **Database schema**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/scripts/schema.ts`\n8. **Seed data**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/scripts/seed-db.ts`\n9. **Test specification**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/docs/tests.md`\n10. **Playwright config**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/playwright.config.ts`\n11. **Existing login tests**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/tests/login.spec.ts`\n12. **Test runner script**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/scripts/test.ts`\n13. **App routing**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/App.tsx`\n14. **Redux store**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/store.ts`\n15. **Netlify config**: `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify.toml`\n16. **Package.json** (with test script): `/repo/apps/LinearClone/package.json`\n\nThis comprehensive structure provides everything needed to write thorough Playwright tests for the sign-up feature, following the patterns established in the existing login tests."}],"totalDurationMs":52371,"totalTokens":56402,"totalToolUseCount":33,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":910,"cache_read_input_tokens":52026,"output_tokens":3465,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":910},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}}}
